---
system: sys-19-billing-subscription
flow_id: order-cancel
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/19-billing-subscription#order-cancel
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, BillingService, Stripe, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - POST /v1/billing/orders/{order_id}/cancel
externals: [Stripe]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - parent_jwt_stale_re_pin_required
  - already_shipped_use_return_flow
  - already_cancelled
  - stripe_void_failed
  - order_not_found
idempotency: X-Request-Id 24h dedup
retry: caller-side exponential backoff on 5xx only
timeout: 5s p99
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant BillingService
    participant Stripe
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over ParentApp: parent in parent_settings → order history taps "Cancel order" on CREATED / PAID / FULFILLING row

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/billing/orders/{order_id}/cancel {X-Request-Id} and parent JWT Bearer
    Gateway->>Gateway: auth-resolver — require parent JWT (ADR-0005 D6 — fresh within 60s)
    alt parent_jwt_stale_re_pin_required
        Note over Gateway: parent JWT issued > 60s ago
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 parent_jwt_stale — re-PIN required
    else authenticated
        Gateway->>BillingService: forward request
        BillingService->>BillingService: verify JWT freshness < 60s (ADR-0005 D6)
        alt order_not_found
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, state, state_version, stripe_payment_intent_id FROM orders WHERE id={order_id} AND household_id={household_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: no rows
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 404 order_not_found
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 404
        else already_cancelled
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, state, state_version FROM orders WHERE id={order_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {state: 'cancelled'}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 409 already_cancelled
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409
        else already_shipped_use_return_flow
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, state, state_version FROM orders WHERE id={order_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {state: 'shipped'|'arrived'|'activated'}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 409 already_shipped_use_return_flow {order_id, return_flow_url: /v1/billing/orders/{order_id}/return-request}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409 — direct to UC-BU16 return/refund flow
        else stripe_void_failed
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, state, state_version, stripe_payment_intent_id FROM orders WHERE id={order_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {state: 'created'|'paid'|'fulfilling', state_version}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE orders SET state='cancel_pending' WHERE id={order_id} AND state_version={sv} (CAS)
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/payment_intents/{stripe_payment_intent_id}/cancel OR POST /v1/refunds {payment_intent: stripe_payment_intent_id}
            Stripe--xBillingService: 5xx / timeout
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE orders SET state='cancel_failed' WHERE id={order_id}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 502 stripe_void_failed
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 502
        else success
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, state, state_version, stripe_payment_intent_id FROM orders WHERE id={order_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {state: 'created'|'paid'|'fulfilling', state_version}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE orders SET state='cancel_pending' WHERE id={order_id} AND state_version={sv} (CAS)
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/payment_intents/{stripe_payment_intent_id}/cancel OR POST /v1/refunds {payment_intent: stripe_payment_intent_id}
            Stripe-->>BillingService: {status: 'canceled'|'succeeded'}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE orders SET state='cancelled', cancelled_at=now(), state_version=state_version+1 WHERE id={order_id}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT audit_logs {action: 'order_cancel', actor_jti, order_id, household_id, ts}
            BillingService-)PostgreSQL: emit order.cancelled event
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {order_id, state: 'cancelled', cancelled_at}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: timeout 5s p99 — X-Request-Id 24h dedup — CAS on state_version prevents concurrent double-cancel — audit_logs row on every mutation
